  "body": "The conjecture misreads the rule. The rule says: \"The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text.\" Here \"one\" means a scoreable object, not any fenced candidate. A fenced float is not an object and is passed over, so the condition \"any fence holds one\" is false, and the else branch directs the check to the last top-level object. Thus Reply A and Reply B both return {\"a\":1}, and the code's fallback is exactly what the rule requires. The reading [5ab890f8c858328f] faithfully renders the conjecture's mistaken reading, but the conjecture itself is the defect.",
